WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们还是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会深度解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.570
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.280
Hey, everybody.
嘿，大家好。

9
00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.640
It is Michael's birthday.
今天是迈克尔的生日。

10
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.660
Michael, it's your B-Day.
迈克尔，今天是你的生日。

11
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.140
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

12
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.280
Oh, Angela, he would be so happy if anyone responded to his birthday like that.
噢，安吉拉，如果有人能这样回应他的生日，他一定会非常开心的。

13
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.400
Yeah, this guy needs a party like nobody else.
是啊，这家伙比谁都渴望一场派对。

14
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.880
He needs the party.
他太需要这场派对了。

15
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.500
It's so true.
确实如此。

16
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:51.140
Guys, it's season two, episode 19, Michael's birthday, written by Lee Eisenberg and Gene Stepnitsky, directed by Ken Whittingham.
各位，这是第二季第19集《迈克尔的生日》，由李·艾森伯格和吉恩·斯图普尼茨基编剧，肯·威廷汉执导。

17
00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.500
Guys, I'm in my closet right now.
伙计们，我现在在我的衣橱里。

18
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.260
I am in my That's What She Should.
我待在我的“那她也该说”录音室里。

19
00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:00.600
This morning, my husband figured out how to try to soundproof it, Sam.
今天早上，我丈夫山姆想办法给这儿做了隔音处理。

20
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.820
I don't know if we did it.
我不知道我们成功了没。

21
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:10.300
We tried, but we got a shower curtain out of the guest room, and Josh put it across the shed and hung some blankets on it.
我们试过了，从客房拿了浴帘，乔希把它横在棚子里，又在上面挂了一些毯子。

22
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.500
We took, you know, the clamps that our kids have a fort building kit?
我们用了孩子们搭建堡垒用的那种夹子，你知道吗？

23
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:14.940
Wow.
哇。

24
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.600
And we took all of their clamps.
我们把他们所有的夹子都拿来了。

25
00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.840
So I hope the kids don't get to do a fort this week because mom is trying to podcast from home.
所以我希望孩子们这周别想搭堡垒了，因为妈妈正在家里录播客。

26
00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:31.440
The best part of seeing you right now on this video chat while we do this is that you are wearing a set of gamer headphones.
现在在视频聊天里看到你，最棒的一点就是你戴着一副游戏耳机。

27
00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:32.720
Yes, I am.
没错，我戴着呢。

28
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.420
I have a giant microphone, but I've pointed it up to the sky.
我有一个巨大的麦克风，但我把它指向了天空。

29
00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:39.100
Like an antenna coming out of your ear.
就像从你耳朵里伸出来的一根天线。

30
00:01:39.420 --> 00:01:40.280
Yeah, that's true.
是啊，确实如此。

31
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.060
And we're going to put a photo of this on the pod.
我们会在播客里放一张这个的照片。

32
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.380
Should I do a summary?
我要做个剧情梗概吗？

33
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:45.460
Here it is.
在这儿呢。

34
00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:46.480
Do a summary, babe.
来个梗概吧，宝贝。

35
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:48.740
I don't know why I called you babe.
我不知道我为什么叫你宝贝。

36
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:49.480
I don't know.
我也不知道。

37
00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:50.620
I don't know either.
我也不知道。

38
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:58.280
It's Michael's birthday, and he is desperate to be the center of attention.
今天是迈克尔的生日，他极度渴望成为众人的焦点。

39
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:05.760
Meanwhile, we learn that Kevin is waiting for the results of a mole biopsy.
与此同时，我们得知凯文正在等待痣活检的结果。

40
00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.160
Yes.
没错。

41
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:07.440
Kevin is very worried.
凯文非常担心。

42
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:14.520
He might have skin cancer, and this is causing a distraction to Michael's birthday that he is unhappy with.
他可能患有皮肤癌，这让迈克尔很不高兴，因为这分散了大家对他生日的注意力。

43
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.200
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

44
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:21.080
Michael's like, today is the day for celebration, and you guys are all worried about Kevin, and I am grumpy about it.
迈克尔觉得，今天是庆祝的日子，你们却都在担心凯文，这让他很不爽。

45
00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:21.440
Yeah.
是啊。

46
00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:22.620
There's my summary.
这就是我的梗概。

47
00:02:23.580 --> 00:02:24.800
I like it, babe.
我很喜欢，宝贝。

48
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.180
Babe, I like it.
宝贝，我很喜欢。

49
00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:27.920
Babe.
宝贝。

50
00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:28.920
Okay, wait.
好吧，等等。

51
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.240
Are we just going to jump right in?
我们这就直接开始吗？

52
00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:31.100
Should we jump right in?
我们要直接开始吗？

53
00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.220
No, there's more summary.
不，还有更多摘要。

54
00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:33.940
And fast facts.
还有快速事实。

55
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:35.580
You've forgotten everything.
你什么都忘了。

56
00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:36.500
Wow.
哇。

57
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:37.440
There's more summary.
还有更多摘要。

58
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:38.600
What is happening?
到底发生了什么？

59
00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:46.900
Also, in this episode, Dwight and Angela really bicker over who exactly is in charge of planning Michael's birthday party.
另外，在这一集中，德怀特和安吉拉为了谁该负责策划迈克尔的生日派对而争吵不休。

60
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:53.140
Is it Dwight as his right-hand man, or is it Angela, head of the PPC?
是作为得力助手的德怀特，还是派对策划委员会负责人的安吉拉？

61
00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:58.100
This is the first time we're going to see a little tension going on between Dwight and Angela.
这是我们第一次看到德怀特和安吉拉之间出现一点紧张气氛。

62
00:02:58.500 --> 00:02:59.020
Yeah.
是啊。

63
00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:04.880
Well, I mean, there was tension in season one over who was the security officer, you know.
嗯，我是说，第一季的时候他们为了谁是安保人员也闹过别扭，你懂的。

64
00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.820
That was pre-them dating.
那是他们交往之前的事了。

65
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:11.500
So they have some issues about who gets to have control of what.
所以他们在谁该掌控什么这件事上一直有些矛盾。

66
00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.800
They had that going into this relationship.
他们在进入这段关系之前就存在这些问题了。

67
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.120
And I have a note card, guys, that says, Dwight and Angela sass.
伙计们，我这儿有张卡片，上面写着：德怀特和安吉拉的互怼。

68
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.400
Ooh, Dwight and Angela sass.
噢，德怀特和安吉拉的互怼。

69
00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.720
All through this episode.
贯穿整集。

70
00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.840
We're going to track it.
我们要追踪一下。

71
00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:28.560
Also in this episode, Jim and Pam, they sneak out of the office together.
这一集里，吉姆和帕姆还一起溜出了办公室。

72
00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:34.040
And in the end, the entire office gang is going to go ice skating.
最后，整个办公室的伙伴们要去滑冰。

73
00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:35.360
Who saw that coming?
谁预料到了这一点？

74
00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:36.580
I didn't see that coming.
我没预料到。

75
00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:40.360
Well, the writers knew that we were going to end up at an ice skating rink.
嗯，编剧们知道我们最终会去滑冰场。

76
00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.460
That leads me into, Sam, please play my special audio clip.
这让我想说，山姆，请播放我的特别音频片段。

77
00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:46.560
Fast facts.
快速事实。

78
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:55.230
Let's submit some little, they're called stings, Angela.
安吉拉，让我们提交一些小片段，它们被称为“刺点”。

79
00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.430
I love that so much.
我太喜欢这个了。

80
00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.050
I didn't even know there was such a thing.
我甚至都不知道还有这种东西。

81
00:03:58.270 --> 00:03:58.490
Yeah.
是啊。

82
00:03:59.030 --> 00:03:59.570
Thank you.
谢谢你。

83
00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:01.750
So more stings, please.
所以，请多来点“刺点”。

84
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.530
More stings, guys.
多来点“刺点”，伙计们。

85
00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:04.690
Send us your stings.
把你们的“刺点”发给我们。

86
00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.590
I didn't even know that was a term.
我甚至都不知道这是个术语。

87
00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.990
We're learning so much.
我们学到了好多。

88
00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:08.730
We're a hundred.
我们一百岁了。

89
00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.650
But thank you for making us stings.
但谢谢你们为我们制作“刺点”。

90
00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:17.730
So fast fact number one is that Steve Carell is a very, very good ice skater.
所以第一个快速事实是，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔是个非常、非常棒的滑冰选手。

91
00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.030
He played hockey growing up.
他从小就打冰球。

92
00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:24.330
He played pickup hockey every week as an adult.
成年后他每周都会参加业余冰球比赛。

93
00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:26.990
Fan question from Matt Loveless.
来自马特·洛夫莱斯的粉丝提问。

94
00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.490
Was the plot built around Steve's ability to ice skate?
剧情是围绕史蒂夫的滑冰能力构建的吗？

95
00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:32.510
Yes.
是的。

96
00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.710
He's so good.
他太厉害了。

97
00:04:33.890 --> 00:04:34.890
He's really good.
他真的很厉害。

98
00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:35.550
Yes.
是的。

99
00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:42.030
The writers had on one of their cards up on the wall this fact about Steve being a good ice skater.
编剧们在墙上的卡片里写过史蒂夫擅长滑冰这个事实。

100
00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:45.550
And they had been looking forever for a way to incorporate it.
他们一直在寻找机会把它融入剧情中。

101
00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:59.330
And you guys might remember that later when we filmed the Threat Level Midnight, that again, that plot of Threat Level Midnight, the movie, takes place in an ice skating rink.
你们可能还记得，后来我们拍摄《午夜威胁》时，那部电影的剧情又一次设定在溜冰场里。

102
00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:04.190
And that was just like another opportunity to feature Steve's ice skating ability.
那正好又是另一个展示史蒂夫溜冰技巧的机会。

103
00:05:04.790 --> 00:05:08.430
I was at the car wash one time waiting for my car to get washed, right?
有一次我在洗车店等车洗好，对吧？

104
00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:13.190
You know, the one you kind of, you can drive through part of it and then you wait on the other side, right?
你知道那种，你可以开车穿过一部分，然后在另一边等着，对吧？

105
00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:13.590
Yeah.
嗯。

106
00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:17.950
So I'm at the car wash and this guy walks up to me and goes, I ice skate with Steve.
我在洗车店的时候，有个家伙走过来对我说，我和史蒂夫一起滑过冰。

107
00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.670
Just, you know, sometimes I ice skate with Steve.
就是，你知道，有时候我会和史蒂夫一起滑冰。

108
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:22.230
And I was like, oh, what?
我当时就想，哦，什么？

109
00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:22.930
Oh, okay.
哦，好吧。

110
00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.730
Well, way to go.
那真不错。

111
00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:28.250
Well, you're probably very good because Steve is good.
那你肯定很厉害，因为史蒂夫很厉害。

112
00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.230
Have a nice day.
祝你今天愉快。

113
00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:34.810
Well, you know, Angela, my husband Lee ice skates, he's on several pickup hockey teaMs.
安吉拉，你知道吗，我丈夫李也滑冰，他参加了好几个业余冰球队。

114
00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:37.330
And my son as well is a hockey player.
我儿子也是个冰球运动员。

115
00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:43.510
And my husband now plays on the pickup team that Steve used to play on.
我丈夫现在就在史蒂夫以前待过的那个业余球队打球。

116
00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.230
I wonder if he plays with the guy from the car wash.
我在想他是不是和洗车店那个家伙一起打球。

117
00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:49.310
Steve does not play pickup hockey anymore.
史蒂夫现在不打业余冰球了。

118
00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.990
He told me he kind of retired from that.
他告诉我他算是退役了。

119
00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.910
But back when we shot this episode, he was really into it.
但在我们拍这一集的时候，他真的很热衷于此。

120
00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.430
He was really into it.
他真的很投入。

121
00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.150
And Jenna, you're like a hockey mom.
珍娜，你简直就是个“冰球妈妈”。

122
00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:03.370
I have been on the ice with you now and I've met your hockey mom friends and I am into it.
我现在和你一起上过冰，也见过你的那些冰球妈妈朋友们，我真的很喜欢。

123
00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.450
I don't have a kid that plays hockey, but they told me you can drink beer at like 10 a.m.
我虽然没有孩子打冰球，但她们告诉我，你可以在早上10点喝啤酒。

124
00:06:08.590 --> 00:06:09.250
hockey matches.
在冰球比赛的时候。

125
00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:12.350
And I'm like, I think this is the crowd I should be in.
我就想，我觉得这才是适合我的圈子。

126
00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:14.150
I mean, I'm over at the soccer field.
我是说，我在足球场那边。

127
00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:16.610
They got nothing at that concession stand.
那里的售货亭什么都没有。

128
00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.050
Maybe some pretzels.
可能只有些椒盐卷饼。

129
00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:22.790
I mean, we're at these hockey rinks sometimes at 7 in the morning or 8 in the morning and
我是说，我们有时早上7点或8点就在这些冰球场了，

130
00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:26.730
they open up that concession stand and they go for it.
他们会打开售货亭，然后就开始畅饮了。

131
00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:33.830
I am not a beer drinker, but I am amazed at people's ability to have a glass of beer in
我不喝啤酒，但我很佩服人们在早上就能喝上一杯啤酒的能力。

132
00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:34.190
the morning.
我在想，那会让我彻底倒下的。

133
00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.010
I'm like, that would do me in.
不过，天哪，我真的很喜欢冰球社区。

134
00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.930
But yeah, oh God, I love the hockey community.
那是一个非常、非常棒的社区。

135
00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:41.310
It's a great, it's a great, great community.
我喜欢成为其中的一员。

136
00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:43.970
I love being a part of it.
好了，第二个速记事实，这是一个来自蕾娜塔的粉丝提问。

137
00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.530
All right, fast fact number two, this is a fan question from Renata.
她说，这一集有几个外景拍摄地。

138
00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:52.750
She said, this episode has several external locations.
是因为这个原因，拍摄这一集花费的时间更长吗？

139
00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:56.910
Did it take longer to produce this episode because of that?
我们通常需要五天时间来拍摄一集，尽管有多个外景地，我们还是能在五天内完成这一集的拍摄。

140
00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:03.110
So we usually would take five days to shoot an episode and we were still able to shoot this
你猜我做了什么，安吉拉？

141
00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.790
episode in five days, even with our multiple locations.
什么？

142
00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:07.650
And guess what I did, Angela?
我从“肯特百科”那里得到了一些关于我们拍摄地点的内幕消息。

143
00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:08.210
What?
肯特·萨博纳克，让我们听听吧。

144
00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:13.130
I got some scoop from Kentopedia about our locations.
好的。

145
00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.170
Kent Sabornak, let's hear it.
首先，吉姆和帕姆去的商店是位于伍德曼大道和谢尔曼路交汇处的一家Rite Aid药店。

146
00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.230
All right.
你还记得那家Rite Aid吗，安吉拉？

